# N4 (Codex OPUS-CODEX-20261015-19: every place, also one in a branch that would not run, must exist and admit): D
# has y, but as an int, and the code declares y a size_t in a branch that does not run. The admission fails when the
# program runs, before x: 1 runs -- the implicit call throw, taken by catch: call; D\x keeps 10. Entry 7.
S:
    int: x 0
    x: 1
    if: x = 2
        size_t: y 5U
end: S
D:
    int: x 10
    int: y 3
end: D
fn: run () int
    int: r 82
    call: S D
    catch: call ()
        r: 83
        if: D\x = 10 && D\y = 3
            r: 7
    ---
return: r
int: got run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
